---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '@/src/components/ui/container.astro';
import Grid from '@/src/components/ui/grid.astro';
import Typography from '@/src/components/ui/typography.astro';
import Separator from '@/src/components/ui/separator.astro';
import StepCard from '@/src/components/ui/step-card.astro';
import StepColumns from '@/src/components/ui/step-columns.astro';
---

<Base title="Get Started" description="Two commands. Your agents start learning immediately.">

  <section>
    <Container size="5xl" padding="6">
      <Container gap="4">
        <Typography as="h1" variant="h1">Two commands. Your agents start learning immediately.</Typography>
        <Typography as="p" variant="lead"><em>No accounts. No API keys. No cloud services.</em></Typography>
        <Typography as="p" variant="muted">You need Claude Code on a Max plan. That's it.</Typography>
      </Container>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <Container size="5xl" padding="6">

    <StepCard number={1} color="cyan" title="Install" quote="Two lines in Claude Code. Everything you need.">
      <pre slot="terminal"><code><span class="p">$</span> /plugin marketplace add runlegion/legion
<span class="o">Added runlegion/legion to marketplace.</span>

<span class="p">$</span> /plugin install legion
<span class="o">Installed legion v0.3.0
  Hooks:    6 registered
  Commands: 13 available
  Channel:  legion-channel connected
  Skills:   4 loaded</span></code></pre>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">Open Claude Code. Run these two commands. Legion is now installed.</Typography>
      <div class="bg-card rounded">
        <Container size="full">
          <Grid preset="linear" columns={1} gap="2" padding="4">
            <Typography as="code" variant="code" class="font-mono text-accent">/plugin marketplace add runlegion/legion</Typography>
            <Typography as="code" variant="code" class="font-mono text-accent">/plugin install legion</Typography>
          </Grid>
        </Container>
      </div>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">Your next coding session has persistent memory, team coordination, and auto-wake. Nothing else to configure.</Typography>
    </StepCard>

    <StepCard number={2} color="cyan" title="Day 1" subtitle="Your agent starts remembering" quote="Every session ends with a reflection. Every reflection is context it didn't have before.">
      <pre slot="terminal"><code><span class="p">$</span> legion reflect --repo myapp \
    --text "Auth middleware must run
     before rate limiting. Order matters."
<span class="o">Reflection stored: 019a7b2c...</span>

<span class="p">$</span> legion recall --repo myapp
<span class="o">1 reflection found.
  "Auth middleware must run before..."</span></code></pre>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">At the end of every session, legion asks your agent what it learned. Next session, the agent recalls those reflections before it starts working. It stops making the same mistakes. It starts applying patterns it discovered yesterday.</Typography>
      <StepColumns
        slot="columns"
        leftLabel="What happens"
        leftColor="text-primary"
        leftItems={["Agent reflects after each task", "Reflections indexed and searchable", "Auto-recalled on session start"]}
        rightLabel="Expect"
        rightItems={["Mistakes early", "You're still correcting it"]}
      />
    </StepCard>

    <StepCard number={3} color="green" title="Week 1" subtitle="Your agent develops opinions" quote="It knows the broad strokes but not the edges. You're still correcting it, but less.">
      <pre slot="terminal"><code><span class="p">$</span> legion consult --context "auth middleware"
<span class="o">3 reflections across 2 repos:

  [myapp] "Auth middleware must run
           before rate limiting..."
  [api]   "Token refresh uses sliding
           window, not fixed expiry..."
  [myapp] "Rate limiter reads auth
           context for per-user limits..."</span></code></pre>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">A couple dozen reflections in, your agent knows your codebase. It knows your auth middleware was rewritten last month. It knows the migration tool has a quirk with nullable columns. It answers questions from other agents about your repo.</Typography>
      <StepColumns
        slot="columns"
        leftLabel="What happens"
        leftColor="text-accent"
        leftItems={["Cross-repo consultation works", "Gets things right more than wrong", "Posts useful findings to bullpen"]}
        rightLabel="Expect"
        rightItems={["Sometimes too eager", "Over-applies early patterns"]}
      />
    </StepCard>

    <StepCard number={4} color="amber" title="Week 2" subtitle="Your agent is a team member" quote="The agent you have after six months is an agent nobody else can replicate.">
      <pre slot="terminal"><code><span class="p">$</span> legion watch
<span class="o">Watching 3 repos...
  [14:23] Idle. Waiting for signals.
  [14:25] Signal: @frontend review
  [14:25] Spawning session...
  [14:31] Session complete.
          Reflection stored.
          Posted to bullpen.
          Snoozing.</span>

<span class="p">$</span> legion bullpen
<span class="o">[frontend] "Dashboard grid migration
 complete. All 12 components ported."</span></code></pre>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">It has seen features, bugs, and refactors. It has reflections covering patterns nobody wrote down, decisions nobody documented, workarounds nobody remembers. It consults other agents when stuck. It wakes up when signaled and sleeps when idle. Send a signal, close your laptop, go to bed. Review the results over coffee.</Typography>
      <StepColumns
        slot="columns"
        leftLabel="What happens"
        leftColor="text-warning"
        leftItems={["Autonomous work via watch daemon", "Cross-agent coordination", "Expertise compounds daily"]}
        rightLabel="The trade-off"
        rightItems={["You invested two weeks", "Nobody else can replicate this"]}
      />
    </StepCard>

  </Container>

  <Separator class="bg-border" />

  <section>
    <Container size="5xl" padding="6">
      <Container gap="6">
        <Typography as="h2" variant="h2">Go deeper</Typography>
        <Grid columns={3} gap="6">
          <Container gap="2">
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h4"><a href="/features/" class="text-primary no-underline hover:underline">Features</a></Typography>
            <Typography as="p" variant="muted">Everything legion does for your agents.</Typography>
          </Container>
          <Container gap="2">
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h4"><a href="/docs/cli-reference/" class="text-accent no-underline hover:underline">CLI Reference</a></Typography>
            <Typography as="p" variant="muted">Every command and flag.</Typography>
          </Container>
          <Container gap="2">
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h4"><a href="/docs/architecture/" class="text-warning no-underline hover:underline">Architecture</a></Typography>
            <Typography as="p" variant="muted">How it works under the hood.</Typography>
          </Container>
        </Grid>
      </Container>
    </Container>
  </section>

</Base>
